      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have ran into a problem with the vrc unity video player as well which I think is related...There is zero documentation on this thing (that I could find), which is pretty terrible. I assumed this can be used to have several speakers playing the very same thing from the video player, but so far I've only gotten any output on \"element 0\" in the list when I tried adding multiple audio sources. It would be very nice to have at least some description of the functionality of this thing in the vrc docs (which are laughably lacking)....",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-09-28T16:56:42.520Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A Common setup for surround sound audio on VRChat video players in SDK2 was to use 6 audio sources, and a video file with 6 audio tracks each directed to their specific audio source.\nOn VRCSDK2 we'd edit the VideoPlayer component in this way (First Picture)\n\nIn SDK3, we have to use the VRCUnityVideoPlayer component, which seems to have the same feature labeled as \"Target Audio Sources\".  I set this to 6 elements and plug in all my audio sources as before (Picture 2)\n\nBut when running, the VideoComponent that VRChat creates only has a single \"Controlled Audio track\" (Picture 3).\n\nWithout this working I'm not sure how we can do surround sound movies.",
